---
description: Open a GitHub PR for every ticket-driven change
alwaysApply: true
---
Do not leave ticket work on a local branch only.

After a code, test, docs, or findings change: commit on a unique feature branch, push that branch, and open a GitHub pull request against `main`. Draft is acceptable; a non-draft open PR is preferred. Use `gh pr create` or the GitHub MCP. Do not wait for the user to create the PR in the browser.

Do not merge unless asked. Do not commit ticket work to `main` or to `fix/influx-dotted-identifiers`.

Exception: the restore-broken-baseline skill is restore-only and must not open a PR.

If the change belongs in `grafana-influxdb-datasource`, open the PR on that repository.
